 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 546572,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/c779fdacc3dd89f9.jpg\" alt=\"A table with the left most column indicated bird species A and B, and the right columns indicating the percent of various food types that make up their diet. Species A consumes 95% insects, 5% nectar, and 0% worms. Species B consumes 92% insects, 3% nectar, and 5% worms.\"></p>\n\n<p>Warblers are a group of small songbirds consisting of many species. The table summarizes data collected on the diets of two species of warblers. \nIn addition, both species A and B use the same types of nesting materials and sites for building nests.</p>\n\n<p>A biologist observes that Species A and Species B primarily inhabit different regions of a forest in western Canada. During a forest fire that wiped out the region it inhabited, Species B fled to the region inhabited by Species A. Predict what is likely to happen to these two species in the future. Explain your reasoning.</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1071446,
     "content_html": "Both the species will survive because of difference in needs for food and nesting space."
    },
    {
     "id": 1071447,
     "content_html": "Species A will increase in population whereas species B will remain same due to the overlapping needs for food and nesting space."
    },
    {
     "id": 1071448,
     "content_html": "Only one of these species will survive in this region due to the difference in needs for food and nesting space. The species that loses will either die off or migrate to another region."
    },
    {
     "id": 1071449,
     "content_html": "Only one of these species will survive in this region due to the overlapping needs for food and nesting space. The species that loses will either die off or migrate to another region."
    }
   ],
